{"id":"00000001794707515438:af8c64c302691a57b026a92cdb4080c4","text":"Production SSR hydration initially failed because web islands were lazy while SSR was eager. The local fix uses matching eager registration and discovers islands through server imports. Rebuilt web SSR now matches hydrated HTML without console errors, and a transitive island updates on click. Static HTML contains the serialized loader payload. The rebuilt iOS bundle contains both direct and transitive registrations. Async hooks after await still produce React invalid-hook errors; true native runtime revival is not yet proven."}
{"id":"00000001794707866175:9f15119cadc81781eb73585597a3d365","text":"Pushed 63c42c74e9344db7221a33cde1db9ce2d64c5667. Production web build and normal hydration pass including a transitive interactive island, static HTML and payload, zero server-walker markers. iOS production bundle includes direct and transitive registrations. Build, check, typecheck and 60 targeted vitest tests pass. Remaining: native runtime revival proof; a simulated newer server island renders fallback but React emits hydration error 418; hooks after await lack the custom guard and emit a generic invalid-hook error."}
{"id":"00000001794707920509:a38c4cf8fc466db3c315739e53d3aa9d","text":"A production iOS-target bundle executed with react-test-renderer and revived an eagerly registered client island into the expected RCTView/RCTText tree. This does not exercise an iOS simulator. Version skew still triggers React 418 while showing the fallback, and async server hooks after await still emit a generic invalid-hook error."}

{"id":"00000001794708049121:bf9d5c7800016a9cc61bf435a3349b5a","text":"Pushed 63c42c74e9344db7221a33cde1db9ce2d64c5667. Remaining failures: when HTML and payload contain a server island absent from the client build, ClientFallback appears but React reports hydration error 418; server hooks called after await emit a generic invalid-hook error. Do not mark Phase 1 complete. Native production bundle ran with react-test-renderer and revived an eagerly registered client module into RCTView/RCTText, but no actual native renderer was exercised. Reproduction sources are on beast2 at /home/ubuntu/.scratch/one-loader-jsx-e2e-r308865 and logs at /home/ubuntu/.scratch/loader-jsx-*."}

{"id":"00000001794720039215:20892eaa7c26ad1f55e5da9cdced64de","text":"Pushed 60e1afc47bce1b8f95e5a8c6efd4535c8b9b6392 to origin/feat/loader-jsx (AsyncLocalStorage server walk isolation + post-commit clientHydrated SkewFallback). Verified on beast2: bun run build, check (4/4), oxlint (0 errors), vitest loaderJSX.test.tsx + clientTreeShakePlugin.test.ts, Playwright browser.mjs (SSR === HYDRATED, click count 2) + skew.mjs (<i>missing island</i>, 0 errors), and iOS buildNativeBundle runtime revival + fallback."}
